  "reason": "The current best (config_018: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat; acc=0.619) shows that adding image features to RNA-only multiprofile avgpool (0.591) yields a modest +0.028 gain. The only fusion method tested so far is concat. Config_019 is an identical setup except it uses weighted fusion instead of concat, making it a clean single-variable A/B test against the current best. This directly tests whether the fusion strategy is a meaningful lever or whether concat is already near-optimal. If weighted outperforms concat, it signals that the image contribution can be amplified and justifies further exploration of weighted-fusion variants (e.g., with ViT-L or scvi). If they are comparable, it rules out fusion as a high-priority axis and redirects budget toward RNA encoder or image encoder choices. Under a limited budget, this low-risk, high-information experiment is the most efficient next step because it resolves a binary question that gates multiple downstream decisions."
